   "file": "content/FMA_4706/tier1.md",
   "text": "The coronary sinus carries oxygen-poor blood from the heart itself into the right atrium. The right atrium is an upper chamber of the heart that receives blood. Most of the heart's veins drain into the coronary sinus. This large, thin-walled vein lies on the back of the heart.",
